From fc01169556c7e84ea3e6126a2f9e8b600a334c1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arlo O'Keeffe <tiger@k5d.de>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:10:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: recover when a registry rejects a BLOB commit it
 completed or lost

ghcr.io can take longer than jib.httpTimeout to commit a large BLOB. The
commit PUT then times out and is retried, and ghcr.io rejects the retry
with 404: BLOB_UPLOAD_UNKNOWN if the first attempt committed the BLOB,
or BLOB_UNKNOWN if the upload was lost.

When a commit fails with either code, check whether the BLOB exists and,
if it does not, upload it once more.

Fixes #4301

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012FfNJJLZ9ysezzEA5ayoSN
